#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059500 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cb13e9d9-19f0-5f39-b9f8-e6e2f8fac433" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Coefficient Matrix of a System of Linear Equations"}] :question/id #uuid "b2196eb1-6691-549b-950a-a9bab6863a70" :question/math-academy-id "e-4683" :question/problem "What is the coefficient matrix for the following system of linear equations?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071100/assets/14671e805c18814b31d0c65d0e53c60aae1cf52c60ad8dd146d8a3f4bc823915.png)" :question/worked-solution "First, we organize the system so that every variable has a coefficient:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071100/assets/e0318c549ab4aa25bf2decb41e45e296406d699706c03aff7ea44724d20edece.png)\n\nThe coefficient matrix consists of the coefficients of the variables:\n\n$$\n\\left\\lbrack\n\t\\matrix {\n\t\t1 & -2 \\\n\t\t0 & 2 \n\t}\n\t\\right\\rbrack\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059501 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f9ccaa5-d69c-584d-946e-0c57b3050160" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Augmented Matrix of a System of Linear Equations"}] :question/id #uuid "b5967dd6-bdf9-5cd0-9639-ec2816d04256" :question/math-academy-id "e-4684" :question/problem "What is the augmented matrix for the following system of linear equations?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071100/assets/a5abba041a61cad76d43d5bb13d0fd4e873eb2daf2282e8d9828b8ab79fe2ba0.png)" :question/worked-solution "First, we organize the system so that the variables are ordered $x,y,z$ on the left-hand side, the constants are on the right-hand side, and every variable has a coefficient:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071100/assets/2f9ae37920ec528a700715658900bbbf3ec4c855767bf06f79d044f488a8bbf2.png)\n\nThe coefficient matrix consists of the coefficients of the variables:\n\n$$\n\\left\\lbrack\n\t\\matrix {\n\t\t1 & 1 & -3 \\\n\t\t-7 & -1 & 1 \\\n                2 & 1 & -2 \n\t}\n\t\\right\\rbrack\n$$\n\nThe augmented matrix  is the coefficient matrix augmented with the column that represents the right-hand sides of the equations:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071100/assets/af1499610c0c312a1f5c50d99967a004ae6b3042c3a88ca20a86f922b28aaaff.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059502 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d7c8f4da-c782-51e0-ac51-87a89f31860d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the System of Equations Associated With an Augmented Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "05942b5f-c165-59c6-8b67-24bc8dd40cca" :question/math-academy-id "e-4685" :question/problem "What would be the system of equations for the following augmented matrix?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071100/assets/4d90e81043121495ae8bb7742400b2c9e705cb7d706f553a6ab2aec44b35d017.png)" :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix consists of two parts: the coefficient matrix and the column of constants.\n\nThe coefficient matrix represents the coefficients in the linear system, while the column of constants represents the constants on the right-hand sides of the equations.\n\nUsing the variables $x$ and $y,$ then, the corresponding system of equations is\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071100/assets/3e7f783023405be3ea79a740998fefac3a6ea909e9903f5ea300a9234ae63003.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059503 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "14d047c8-f032-5ff3-aced-65d40bfeeaad" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Augmented Matrix of a Linear System With Variables Other Than x, y, z"}] :question/id #uuid "161a4327-2356-5779-92a6-8495cfffefb9" :question/math-academy-id "e-4686" :question/problem "What is the augmented matrix for the following system of linear equations?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071100/assets/d89417b7eb2d000bbd81fcf4a89ca7eaa5529fc56d9b41bf6e8bb237d2eb9e16.png)" :question/worked-solution "First, we organize the system so that the variables are ordered $a,b,c,d$ on the left-hand side, the constants are on the right-hand side, and every variable has a coefficient:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071100/assets/93874fa93cfd9ef3df1492bbc35056c2381157740d8ca26b475474faf54ee4d1.png)\n\nThe coefficient matrix consists of the coefficients of the variables:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & \\frac{1}{2} & 0 \\\\ -1 & 3 & -4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe augmented matrix is the coefficient matrix augmented with the column that represents the right-hand sides of the equations:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071100/assets/8356d9148bc06d76a5aee41e4a07651c43d94b2496d9542eb8b6e01ee52ea161.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186370774 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cb13e9d9-19f0-5f39-b9f8-e6e2f8fac433" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Coefficient Matrix of a System of Linear Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bc6fa628-503c-566b-9675-8b8c60d0ebba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 7 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370776} {:answer/id #uuid "a9f709d0-4c94-5cf9-8294-fa2e7589c003" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370777} {:answer/id #uuid "9a5abb20-5f90-551e-bc28-c9114def3b6a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 7 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370778} {:answer/id #uuid "c162c19a-4387-539b-90ce-b05ef3c52093" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 7 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370779} {:answer/id #uuid "954c3990-2759-5dc8-bc42-70d4bae35172" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370780}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "954c3990-2759-5dc8-bc42-70d4bae35172" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370780} :answer-field/id #uuid "f574a960-46c6-5658-bc41-f8f052b69dfc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370775}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6b11cca0-0686-5fea-b36d-b3d61cf9d237" :question/math-academy-id "q-1050" :question/problem "What is the coefficient matrix for the following system of equations?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}x+3y=7 \\\\ 2x=4\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we organize the system so that the variables are ordered  $x,y$ \n on the left-hand side, the constants are on the right-hand side, and every variable has a coefficient:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+3y=7 \\\\ 2x+0y=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe coefficient matrix consists of the coefficients of the variables:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059894 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f9ccaa5-d69c-584d-946e-0c57b3050160" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Augmented Matrix of a System of Linear Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "83e807b6-d6f8-53f2-b115-1555aaea5385" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 1 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1 & 9\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056085} {:answer/id #uuid 